<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
Container migration manifest (macOS only; the project filters it out of the iOS app). macOS reads
it once, when it creates the app's sandbox container on the first launch of a sandboxed (signed)
build, and MOVES these items from the user's Library into the container, to the same relative
place. Missing items are skipped. If the container already exists, nothing happens. See
docs/development/index.md, "Sandbox": take a backup and run the pre-check before the first signed
launch, and never delete the container of de.patrickklein.DocumentArchive.

Only Apple's variables (${ApplicationSupport}, ${Library}, ...); there is no ${Preferences}.
Not moved: Ablage.* (LegacyMigration's source, left in place as a backup; the migratedFromAblage
flag travels inside the preferences plist). ContainerMigrationTests check this list.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<key>Move</key>
	<array>
		<!-- The store (ArchiveStore.storeName) with its external PDF data. -->
		<string>${ApplicationSupport}/DocumentArchive.store</string>
		<string>${ApplicationSupport}/DocumentArchive.store-wal</string>
		<string>${ApplicationSupport}/DocumentArchive.store-shm</string>
		<string>${ApplicationSupport}/.DocumentArchive_SUPPORT</string>
		<!-- The fallback store of ArchiveStore.makeContainer, if it was ever created. -->
		<string>${ApplicationSupport}/DocumentArchive-lokal.store</string>
		<string>${ApplicationSupport}/DocumentArchive-lokal.store-wal</string>
		<string>${ApplicationSupport}/DocumentArchive-lokal.store-shm</string>
		<string>${ApplicationSupport}/.DocumentArchive-lokal_SUPPORT</string>
		<!-- The folder copy's bookkeeping (ArchiveMirrorStateStore.fileName). -->
		<string>${ApplicationSupport}/ArchiveMirror.json</string>
		<!-- The settings, where cfprefsd reads them inside the container. -->
		<string>${Library}/Preferences/de.patrickklein.DocumentArchive.plist</string>
	</array>
</dict>
</plist>
